Rule Requirement Default dialect A schema without <code>$schema</code> is JSON Schema 2020-12 Explicit dialect A schema MAY include <code>$schema</code> to use a different dialect (e.g. draft-07) Mandatory support Implementations MUST support at least 2020-12 Recommendation Implementors are RECOMMENDED to use 2020-12 Validation Schemas MUST be valid for their declared or default dialect; unsupported dialects must be handled gracefully, returning an error Documentation Implementations SHOULD document which additional dialects they support <p>A 2020-12 schema (no <code>$schema</code> needed):</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "name": { "type": "string" },
    "age": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 }
  },
  "required": ["name"]
}
</code></pre> <p>The same schema declared explicitly as draft-07:</p> <pre><code>{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "name": { "type": "string" },
    "age": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 }
  },
  "required": ["name"]
}
</code></pre>

